"The postoperative pathology revealed a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) diagnosis with pathological stage pT2. A key adverse finding was positive surgical margins, as noted in the surgical pathology report: \"surgical margins were positive.\" Countervailing findings include the absence of extraprostatic extension and no invasion of the seminal vesicles, as stated: \"the seminal vesicles were not invaded.\" Nodal status is uncertain as no lymph nodes were removed, meaning pNx does not establish node-negative disease, which widens the uncertainty regarding regional disease control. The biopsy confirmed Acinar adenocarcinoma. Postoperative PSA is not recorded, so biochemical recurrence cannot be assessed. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory is essential to revise the prognosis. Missing nodal sampling limits staging and does not establish node-negative disease. The fixed estimated horizon is 39.17 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 25.46–52.87 months; its coverage has not been validated."
